# The Vercel deployment is the dashboard only -- a single self-contained
# static HTML file (dashboard/index.html, generated by
# dashboard/build_dashboard.py, base64 fonts/logo inlined, no build step).
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST, not an exclusion list: everything is ignored by
# default, and only dashboard/ is let back in. A previous version tried to
# enumerate exclusions (corpus/, engine/, etc.) and missed requirements.txt
# at the repo root -- its mere presence made Vercel auto-detect this as a
# Python project and look for a serverless entrypoint that doesn't exist.
# An allowlist can't have that failure mode: a new root-level file (another
# requirements.txt, a package.json, anything) can never silently reach the
# upload and retrigger framework auto-detection again.
*
!dashboard
!dashboard/**
